WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.810
And today, I'm going to talk
about external tools in Canvas.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.430
Since we started
using Canvas, we've

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.340
been experimenting with
a lot of external tools.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.560
And external tools
are the tools that

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.240
are available through Canvas.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.070
So it could be any other tool,
or developed by our developers

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.030
at the school, that we
access them through Canvas.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:30.670
So most of these integration
are available through the course

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:31.690
navigation.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.400
And I'm going to
show some examples.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.890
Some of the integrations
that, when you access to them,

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.590
they are on the
left navigation bar,

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.420
so you can access through that.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.030
Some of them are available
through assignments.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.150
So if you're using a
specific tool, external tool,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.240
you can only access them
through assignments.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.550
And some of the
examples are here,

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.020
like MobLab and Critiquett.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.450
Some of them are
available through modules.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.080
So in order to use those
tools, you have to use modules.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:04.660
And also, HTML editor that we
are using right now, Warpwire.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.880
And I'm going to show that.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.980
And we also experimented
by integrating these tools

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.500
within the sub account
and within courses.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.830
So we tried different levels
of integrations, also.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:23.500
So past and current--
so far, we use Warpwire.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.120
We name it.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.620
It shows on the
left navigation bar,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.310
and we name it Course Videos.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.180
Warpwire is our media platform.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.300
So instead of Panopto, School
of Management is using Warpwire.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:41.200
And this is how we are accessing
Warpwire from within Canvas.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.450
So basically, I'm
just going to, maybe--

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.120
so you can see it here.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.960
It's on the left navigation.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.390
And then, students, or
users and instructors,

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.790
when they click on
it, they are accessing

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.250
Warpwire within Canvas.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.860
And it's already integrated.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.520
They don't have to go to another
platform to use the platform,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:07.800
they just, within Canvas,
access to this platform.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.410
So I'll go to the next one.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.210
SOM Syllabus,
that's another tool

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.330
that they will opt at
the School of Management

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.450
to have access to our syllabi
on a different platform.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.420
So I'm going to
show an example too.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.390
And hopefully, we will be
retiring that tool soon,

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.630
because we are going to
go back to the syllabus

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.840
available within Canvas.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.430
So if a user clicks
on the SOM Syllabus,

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.380
they have access to
the syllabus that

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.730
is actually hosted in another
platform, called Confluence.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.010
So again, without
leaving Canvas,

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.500
by clicking on that
link, they access to it.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.300
And they don't have to sign in.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.490
They don't have to enter
any user name or password.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.640
Roster-- Roster too was
developed by S1 developers

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.450
also.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:00.510
We since then retired it,
because now, the university

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.970
has a really good photo
roster that we can use.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.840
But before university
had a roster,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.510
we created our own
with the pictures,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.930
and with the name of the
students and their emails.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.870
We are not using it any
more, but that's another tool

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.990
that we developed and
we've been using in Canvas.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.260
And VoiceThread-- again,
while integrating Canvas,

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.630
we integrated a lot of tools.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.690
And one of the tools that we
tried out was VoiceThread.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.160
And VoiceThread is an online
platform for providing feedback

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.270
on the media files.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:37.440
And the feedback can be an
audio file, video file, text,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.530
and any type of file
that you can share.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.350
So I'm going to click on it,
so you see how we access it.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:47.650
But since then, we stopped
paying for the VoiceThread

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.740
license, so we don't
have any access to it.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.930
But again, VoiceThread
was available

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.650
on the left navigation bar,
as well as in Assignments.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.830
So we could create
assignments and have

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.720
students access VoiceThread.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.330
Or we were using it on
the left navigation bar,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:07.170
so our users would just click
on it, and go to VoiceThread,

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.300
without entering their
username and password.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.330
So these are the ones
that we've been using.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.550
And these are tested.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:21.840
So when I say tested, I mean,
we hear about these tools,

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.180
and we read about them, and we
investigate, and we implement

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.220
it, sometimes, at
[INAUDIBLE] level,

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.310
sometimes, at the
sandbox, at course level.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.920
I try to do it mostly
at the course level.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.140
These are some of the
ones that we tested.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.810
And we decided that
it's not ready yet.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.080
It's not working as much as
we want them to be working.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.580
There are some issues with them.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.910
So we are still either
trying to decide,

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.960
or decided not to pursue.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.470
So one of them is
called Turnitin.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.940
You're all familiar
with Turnitin.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.190
It's a plagiarism tool.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.650
And we are using it externally.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:02.280
So our faculty and staff
members are going to Turnitin

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.960
and uploading all
these documents.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.210
So we were thinking
it would be helpful

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:09.000
if you provide this
access within Canvas.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.865
Unfortunately,
right now, you see

00:05:10.865 --> 00:05:14.640
error, because my test
account is expired.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.990
We had some issues with it.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.220
It wasn't 100% accurate.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:22.830
It works better externally,
as another platform,

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.540
rather than within Canvas.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.960
So we are still trying to
decide if we should just

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:34.320
ask our users to use an external
platform, or use within Canvas.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.000
The next one that
we are testing is--

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.130
actually, we did already.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.820
We are not pursuing it,
because library just

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.160
made a presentation, so we
are one of the schools using

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.950
Ares system heavily.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:52.200
So if you were to use Harvard
Business Publishing LTI, that

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:55.500
would mean our students
would go to course files,

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.680
and then toward course reserves,
and then Harvard cases.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.080
So they would have to go
to three different places

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.430
to get one course material.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.730
So we decided that,
unless it integrates

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.520
with course resources
or files, we are not

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:09.780
going to use Harvard cases.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.410
So we decided not to.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:13.380
I don't have any
access to it right now.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.330
Study.Net-- just another one.

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.550
I don't know if you're
familiar with Study.Net.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:20.730
Study.net allows faculty
members, instructors,

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.890
to create their course packs.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.660
It could be a web
site, it could be

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.420
a file of their
own creation, or it

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.710
could be a case that is
developed and presented

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.510
by any other business school.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:37.510
So we also tested it.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.220
And we decided that
we are not going

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:43.750
to go with it, because just like
with Harvard Business cases,

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.690
this required our
students and faculty

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:50.590
to go to yet another place.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.750
Here, right now,
currently, they only

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:58.060
go to files and course
reserves, which is down there.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.490
But if they were
to use Study.Net,

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.560
then they would also
have to go to Study.Net

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.370
to get some of the files.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.130
So we are looking
for a solution that

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.660
will allow us to put all the
resources in one place, so

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.220
our students and
faculty, they don't

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.500
have to go to three or
four different places.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.600
We haven't found it
yet, but we are looking

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.690
and continue to look.

00:07:20.955 --> 00:07:23.400
So currently being tested--

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.340
so our last two tools
that are currently

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.860
being tested and piloted--

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.960
one of them is CritiqueIt.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:32.090
It was introduced by CTL.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.540
So after investigating
it, I introduced it

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.350
to one of our faculty members.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:39.740
He has used it for
his spring class.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:43.160
And he actually--
for CritiqueIt,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.280
as I mentioned
before, some tools

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:47.750
are available
within assignments.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:50.880
So CritiqueIt is available
only through Assignments.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.260
So if you decide
to use a tools that

00:07:54.260 --> 00:08:01.230
allows faculty instructors
to use this tool,

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.590
so we have to use CritiqueIt
through Assignments.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:06.900
So when they create
an assignment,

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.930
and they select External
Tool, and students

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:14.370
if they need to use it, they
go through the Assignments.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.700
And CritiqueIt is an
online critiquing tool

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.800
that allows instructors to--

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.380
or users, I should say,
because students can also

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:23.970
upload files--

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:28.380
they can upload their images or
their videos, or even like Word

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.920
files, and people can
give comments on them.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:36.155
They can record videos, and they
can provide comments on them.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.960
I'm going really fast,
but you can ask me more,

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.630
because we have a
couple of minutes left.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:50.610
So currently, we are
also testing VeriCite.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.070
I mentioned our
issues with Turnitin,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:57.290
so we are investigating another
online plagiarism tool called

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.080
VeriCite and trying to see if
it works better within Canvas.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.820
So we are currently testing it.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:06.300
So we've been doing some tests.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.380
And if we decide,
OK, this is better,

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.650
then I'm going to
ask a faculty member

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.030
to pilot it for next fall.

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.870
And then, we will be able
to decide after the pilot

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.280
if we're going to go
with the tool or not.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.960
So again, it's via Assignments.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.450
I select External
Tool, select VeriCite.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:29.210
So students when they're
uploading their files,

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.660
assignment files,
they go within Canvas,

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.330
but they're actually
uploading in VeriCite.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:38.260
And faculty can access,
also, from Canvas.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:49.010
Finally, coming soon-- so this
is the tool that we tested

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.350
and we piloted.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.840
We didn't pilot within Canvas,
but we piloted outside.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.150
And we decided to go with it.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.590
It's called MobLab.

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:02.040
It's an online gaming for
economics and business cases.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.080
So we are going to start
using it next fall.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.090
And just like I
mentioned before,

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:10.970
MobLab is available through
Assignments or Modules.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:15.860
So a person who
presented about modules--

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:20.510
so we can put MobLab games and
activities under each module.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.960
It allows us to do that.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.260
So as you can see,
first, we activate it.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.430
So that's one thing.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.910
Some of the external
tools require activation.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:32.040
So we require students
to click there first,

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.680
to activate their account.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.110
And then they access
through SOM icon.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.870
And now, their account
is activated in MobLab.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:39.920
They can start using it.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:44.870
So we can start weekly modules
and add MobLab games for them

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.535
to access it.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.970
And thank you.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:57.440
Any questions?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.260
Yes?

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.870
So are these platforms
that you've developed?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:02.620
Some of them.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:04.660
Like the syllabus,
that, we developed.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.280
And roster, we developed.

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:09.670
But MobLab, VeriCite,
Turnitin, it's

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:12.130
developed by the companies.

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:15.210
So I need to have a sign up
tool for my students for labs.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.320
And the scheduler
in Canvas doesn't

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:18.740
work for what I need to do.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.740
So I'm learning how to do it
in a data-based platform called

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:22.990
Airtable.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:26.570
And it has an API, but the
students don't have access to--

00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:29.060
I don't have access to the
roster and their schedule

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:29.640
and so forth.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.980
So they have to get an
account on a separate platform

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:32.930
and so forth.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:37.030
So it would be great if I could
get the roster information

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:42.694
and so forth or the Airtable
tool into the Canvas API.

00:11:42.694 --> 00:11:43.402
So can I do that?

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:44.880
[LAUGHTER]

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:48.190
You need to contact Pilar
and her team, I think.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:53.510
We worked with them to
create our own tools for SOM,

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.190
but you have to check with them.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.890
So all the databases that
we use for the roster

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:59.416
came from S1 databases.

00:11:59.416 --> 00:11:59.915
Yeah.

00:11:59.915 --> 00:12:01.623
So it sounds like it
worked for you then.

00:12:01.623 --> 00:12:02.510
It worked, yes.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.280
And there's also
some Canvas groups

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:08.870
that they do share their
resources and developments

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.010
on GitHub.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.790
So you may find something
like that already developed,

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.180
and you just modify it
to your own purposes.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:19.130
I'd say the roster was tricky,
because our developers were

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.560
pulling information that always
was inaccurate to Banner.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:25.418
So in the People
tool, and then I

00:12:25.418 --> 00:12:27.301
know that the Roster
tool that we use now,

00:12:27.301 --> 00:12:29.210
it was calling
different students.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:29.710
Yeah.

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:32.091
So It's tricky, but I
think it's all sorted out.

00:12:32.091 --> 00:12:32.590
Yeah.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.330
OK.

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.040
One other comment.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:40.720
There's a web
site, EduAppCenter,

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:45.040
that lists over 200
externally developed tools

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.200
for various things
that are already

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.900
plug-and-play for Canvas.

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.750
That's not to say that you can
just immediately plug it in.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.270
We have some protocols
for actually checking

00:12:55.270 --> 00:13:00.070
to make sure that any data
shared with an external vendor

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:03.310
is secure, because of FERPA
and that sort of thing.

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.950
But you might very well
find an application

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.220
that does what you're looking
for on the EduAppCenter.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.770
And then you can contact the
Canvas group and say, hey,

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.831
